687 0 obj
<<
/Title (Problem: an IP address has two roles - identifying a host and indicating its location \(the network prefix\). When a device moves to another network its address no longer matches the local prefix, so packets are routed to the old network and the device would need a new address, which breaks ongoing TCP connections. Mobile IP \(RFC 5944 for IPv4\) lets a device keep its permanent address while moving, so applications are not interrupted.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 630 0 R
/Next 750 0 R
>>
